# Rust / cargo build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Packaged crate tarballs - `crate-dist/` is what the proto compiler image copies back,
# `*.crate` is what a local `cargo package` produces.
crate-dist/
*.crate

# Staging directory that `make generate_ondewo_protos` feeds to the compiler image as
# /input-volume; it is removed again when generation succeeds.
.proto-input/

# Scratch file of `make check_build`
build_check.txt

# Credentials clone of `make ondewo_release`
ondewo-devops-accounts/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Generated by MacOS
.DS_Store

# Generated by Windows
Thumbs.db

# NOTE - deliberately NOT ignored:
#  * src/api/     the generated stubs. They are the published library, so they are committed
#                 exactly like the generated code of the python and typescript clients: a
#                 consumer installs this crate from crates.io and never runs the generator.
#  * Cargo.lock   the compiler image ships the lockfile it resolved, which is what makes a
#                 build of this crate reproducible.
